# Compact admin layout

When creating or changing **admin** forms, tables, toolbars, or config pages:

1. **Same line first** — Put related fields on one row when they fit at desktop width (dropdowns, SKUs, prices, units, toggles, paired URLs, icon + search/select).
2. **Full width only when needed** — Long URLs, multi-line descriptions, rich text, and primary content blocks may span 100%.
3. **Reuse existing grids** — See `docs/UI_GUIDELINES.md` §6 (`.admin-form-grid-2`, `.mat-form-grid-details`, `.mat-form-url-row`, `.fq-catalog-picker-wrap`, `.fq-catalog-picker`) before adding new layout classes.
4. **Responsive stack** — Collapse to fewer columns at documented breakpoints (≤1200px / ≤768px); do not default to single-column desktop layouts.
5. **Helper text** — Keep under the row or drop redundant copy; avoid helper paragraphs that force extra vertical space between controls on the same logical row.

Goal: shorter pages, less scrolling, faster scanning.
